                <pb facs="0830" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg732"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Draper.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay directs that proper authorities be informed of the expected arrival of
                    the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Dixie</hi> at Naples April 6, Venice April
                    30, and Livorno May 9; and that port courtesies usual in such cases be
                    suggested.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
